schema: agent.current_status
schema_version: "1.0"

metadata:
  plan_id: gauntlet-impl              # stable slug, matches evidence dir name
  plan_version: "2.0.0"
  spec_id: Core-spec                  # usually == plan_id; differs if one spec
                                      # drives multiple plans
  spec_version: "2.0.0"
  initialized: true                   # false only before the very first burst
  last_updated: "2026-08-27"
  updated_by: "orchestrator (Task 13 implementation COMPLETE, all gates green, uncommitted; one blind confirmation round + closure remain — clean handoff)"

execution:
  last_settled_task: task12           # most recent task with a CONFIRM in
                                      # latest_evidence; null if none yet
  in_flight_task: task13              # the ONE task currently being worked;
                                      # null if nothing is in flight.
                                      # task13's IMPLEMENTATION is complete —
                                      # it is in flight only for its CLOSURE
                                      # phase (the task13-closure step in
                                      # next_action: blind confirmation →
                                      # settlement mechanics)
  ready_tasks:                        # tasks whose deps are all settled and
    - task14                          # which are not yet started. Recompute
    - task15                          # this every time a task settles. NOTE:
    - task16                          # dep-satisfied but NOT workable while
    - task18                          # task13's closure is in flight (one
                                      # task at a time; task14 is the next
                                      # work task after task13 settles).
  blocked_tasks:
    task17: [task15, task16]          # needs task5 (done) and task15 or task16
    task19: [task18]                  # needs task18
    task20: [task13, task14, task17]  # needs tasks 7, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 17
    task21: [task20]
    task22: [task20]
    task23: [task22]
    task24: [task20]
    task25: [task20]
    task26: [task25]
    task27: [task26]
  plan_blocked: false                 # true only if NOTHING is workable
                                      # (every ready path is blocked)
  plan_blocker: null                  # if plan_blocked, name the single thing
                                      # unblocking it; else null

active:
  task: task13                        # should match execution.in_flight_task
  phase: closure                      # implementation COMPLETE; the in-flight
                                      # work is the confirm-and-close
                                      # procedure (next_action: task13-closure)
  blocker: >-
    What blocks task13's SETTLEMENT (nothing blocks its implementation — that is
    complete and every gate is green on the uncommitted working tree): the ONE
    fresh blind confirmation round, then the closure mechanics. Landed and
    verified: B1 ports settlement surface + earned admissions (committed in
    62d1a5f); B2 settle:: service (all five 16.1 conditions, 16.3 commit order,
    18.3 resume completion, 21.3 dispositions, AK-062 no-bypass half); B3
    single-writer arch rule (boundaries 197→215) + arch-relitigation (all four
    items HOLD); B4 proofs p7_recovery / p11_critic_is_not_verifier /
    g10_builder_writes_answer_key (12/12, teeth in teeth-b4.md); early
    adversarial probe (1C+5M+5m) → correction round 1 (COR-1..7); blind critic
    round 1 (spec NOT-CONFIRM narrow + falsifier 1C/3M/3m) → correction round
    2 (COR2-1..6, incl. the F-1 double-settlement closure at both the admission
    and completion layers). FINAL BATTERY: ports 105/105, app 330/330, sqlite
    48/48, proofs 12/12, standing battery 33/33, lint 0, boundaries 215/215,
    deny ok, ruler PASS, prereg-check 13 PASS (frozen d949e1e0). Full
    slice-by-slice state and every recovery record:
    .agents/reports/task13/IN-FLIGHT.md (read FIRST) and the task13
    checkpoints files.

