observations:
  # Facts a resuming agent needs and shouldn't have to re-derive. Keep this
  # list short and load-bearing — not a running commentary.
  - status: OBSERVED                 # OBSERVED = directly verified this
                                      # session/burst, evidence attached
    statement: "Ruler is frozen with SHA256 digests locked in .gauntlet/reference.lock (answer key sha256:ccc7c99b…, manifest sha256:95331d3e…) and passes `just ruler`."
    evidence: ".gauntlet/reference.lock"
  - status: OBSERVED
    statement: "Tasks 0–12 are closed (their closure-era gates are recorded in .agents/CURRENT_STATUS.md); on the CURRENT tree carrying Task 13, every gate is green with boundaries grown 197→215/215 (the B3 single-writer rule) and the full battery re-run personally 2026-08-27."
    evidence: ".agents/reports/task13/correction-checkpoints.md"
  - status: OBSERVED
    statement: "Task 13 targets AK-040, AK-041, AK-042, AK-043, AK-062 (service-level), AK-031, AK-024 (settle-time half), AK-053; preregistration is frozen at .agents/research/preregistrations/task-13.prereg.yaml (sha256 d949e1e0…)."
    evidence: ".agents/reports/task13/IN-FLIGHT.md"
  - status: OBSERVED
    statement: "Host environment is WSL2 (6 cores, 7.8 GiB RAM, ~1.6 GiB free memory constraint), rustc/cargo 1.98.0, bwrap 0.11.1 only (no docker/podman/qemu/firecracker)."
    evidence: ".agents/reports/environment.json"
  - status: OBSERVED
    statement: "Answer-key unit status: 0 proven settled. 27 provisional through Task 12 (AK-001, AK-002, AK-004, AK-005, AK-015, AK-016, AK-017, AK-018, AK-019, AK-021, AK-022, AK-023, AK-024, AK-025, AK-028, AK-029, AK-030, AK-035, AK-036, AK-037, AK-038, AK-039, AK-049, AK-051, AK-052, AK-054, AK-059). Task 13's confirmation + closure will add its targets to provisional (AK-040, AK-041, AK-042, AK-043, AK-062 service-half, AK-031, AK-053; AK-024's settle-time half upgrades its recorded scope) — the closure record must recompute these counts; do not recompute before the confirmation CONFIRMS. 48 proposed, 0 blocked, 0 unknown."
    evidence: ".agents/reports/reference-candidates.md"
  - status: OBSERVED
    statement: "Sub-agent session interruptions / usage limits have occurred 19 times across tasks 3–13; the tree-outranks-record reconciliation rule must be run before treating any task as unstarted."
    evidence: ".agents/lessons/session-interruption-recovery.md"
  - status: OBSERVED
    statement: "Task 13 final battery on the uncommitted tree (run personally 2026-08-27): ports 105/105, app 330/330, sqlite 48/48, proofs p7/p11/g10 12/12, standing battery p4/p6/p12/p2/p3 33/33, lint 0, boundaries 215/215, deny ok, ruler PASS."
    evidence: ".agents/reports/task13/correction-checkpoints.md"
  - status: OBSERVED
    statement: "The operator's installed role agents (builder, critic, falsifier, finisher, etc.) are NOT invocable from the session's Agent tool ('Agent type not found; available: general-purpose, Explore') — role semantics are carried by the dispatch prompts; re-probe after any client update."
    evidence: ".agents/reports/task13/IN-FLIGHT.md"
  - status: UNKNOWN                  # UNKNOWN = known gap, not yet verified
                                      # either way — do not upgrade to
                                      # OBSERVED without actually checking
    statement: "UNK-001: which containment backend cross_cutting runs under in real use beyond this host's bwrap-only environment."
    evidence: ".wayfinder/reference.yaml"
  - status: UNKNOWN
    statement: "UNK-002: whether this repository should carry a LICENSE, and which."
    evidence: ".wayfinder/reference.yaml"
  - status: UNKNOWN
    statement: "UNK-003: which concrete AgentRunner is runners.default in GAUNTLET.md (deferred to Tasks 15–16)."
    evidence: ".wayfinder/reference.yaml"

next_action:
  task: task13-closure                # NOT task13 implementation — that is
                                      # complete; this step is the confirm +
                                      # close procedure for it
  action: >-
    Step 1 — confirm: run `just ruler` and `scripts/reconcile-checkpoints.sh 13`, then dispatch
    ONE fresh blind confirmation round over the COMPLETE Task-13 surface (two read-only agents —
    spec critic + falsifier roles; prompt shapes in .agents/reports/task13/critic-round1.md's
    header; blind = no task13/** reports access). Step 2 — on CONFIRM, close: orchestrator teeth
    re-verification, paste the ready reference-candidates entries (closure-research drafts + the
    M-1 minimum_reliability entry from early-probe-adjudication.md), write task-13.outcome.yaml
    per TEMPLATE (P2/P4 fired ×3 — early probe, critic round 1; record P1/P3/P5 from the
    checkpoints), write the closure record, then ONE commit with EXPLICIT PATHSPECS (never stage
    .jolli/, .tmp/, .agents/prompts/, AGENTS.md, or the operator's uncommitted files:
    .agents/AGENTS.md, .agents/CURRENT_STATUS.yml, .agents/research/AGENT.md,
    prereg-postrun-schema.md, TEMPLATE.prereg.yaml, escalations.md, lessons files). Then mark
    task13 settled, recompute the DAG (task14 becomes the next ready task), stop, hand off.
    On REVISE: correction round 3 per the finding, rerun gates, reconfirm.
  reason: >-
    Task 13's implementation, both correction rounds, and every gate are complete and verified;
    what remains is the settlement procedure itself — independent blind confirmation, then the
    closure mechanics — all staged in .agents/reports/task13/. After task13 settles, the next
    work task is task14 (Authority gate, sandbox port, tier policies — P5).

handoff:
  settled_summary:
    # One line per settled task or logical group of settled tasks. Prior
    # groups can be batched ("T00 baseline; T01 X; T02 Y"); the most
    # recently settled task gets its own line with enough detail that a
    # resuming agent doesn't need to open its evidence dir just to know
    # what it did.
    - "T00 baseline & delegation spike (76e491a); T01 frozen ruler & digest lock (bf09a30); T02 16-crate workspace skeleton, justfile, boundaries suite 183/183 (1578dde)"
    - "T03 full §5.2/§5.3 domain model, zero dependencies, typed errors (cb2f4ac)"
    - "T04 17 port traits with typed errors, role_result@v1 envelope, 17 shared contract suites with teeth (b27b152)"
    - "T05 config resolution (defaults < GAUNTLET.md < env < flags), §8.6 defaults, doctor checks, gauntlet doctor CLI (610a615)"
    - "T06 rusqlite EventLog + StateStore, content-addressed FsEvidenceStore, state::export canonical service, abort crash helper (86d5be0)"
    - "T07 ReferenceProvider normalize/digest/freeze/verify, doctor check 2 deep parse, gauntlet reference digest CLI, composed P1 proof (ff1ad06)"
    - "T08 gauntlet-adapter-agent-mock, DeterministicClock, SeededIdGenerator, 8 required fixtures, AK-059 pin, 9 playback tests (c4e58fa)"
    - "T09 5 observation facet adapters, facet_evidence@v1 strict codec, gauntlet-app observation::{bundle,digest,input,assembly}, composed proofs p3 and g6 (20d5173)"
    - "T10 comparator & envelope builder, RunComparisonAuthority durable provenance, AdmittedComparison capability, P2 blindness assertion (1dab05c)"
    - "T11 Verifier and evidence binding, examined-bytes binding, composition-seal pin, composed p12 proof (a507d08, 793d115)"
    - "T12 Controller: selection, budget, diagnosis, BudgetMeter/MeteredBudget, ReviewDeps critic-metering, composed proofs p4 and p6, 7 teeth (1a88b39)"
  unresolved_summary:
    # Every open thread that isn't captured elsewhere: outstanding
    # confirmations, deferred scope, stale docs owed a refresh, known
    # follow-ups tied to a later task ID.
    - "Task 13 remaining: ONE fresh blind confirmation round + closure mechanics (teeth re-verify, reference-candidates paste, outcome.yaml, closure record, single commit) — resolves in Task 13"
    - "Task 13 later-scope (adjudicated, triggers recorded): M-1 minimum_reliability run-level conjunct (reference candidate — the frozen ruler's field is §19.2 promotion prose, not machine-countable), M-2/F-2 AK-062 operator-action positive half (Task 21), F-3 admit→commit TOCTOU (Task 15/20 concurrency), F-4 transient non-in-flight edit window, F-7 recovery-time digest (non-content-addressed adapter), m-1/2/4/6/7/8/9/11 minors (critic-round1.md)"
    - "Task 13 partially-composed inherited residuals: L3 settlement crash-window replay COMPOSED; settlement-side sqlite coercions COMPOSED; L2 resume legs composed, retry-ledger persistence remains ports-revision-bound; §21.3 non-integrity failures composed (answer-key read + poll transport)"
    - "Task 14 deferrals: L1 authority-gate + tier posture, runner capability-vs-tier dispatch check, mock capability honesty pin"
    - "Tasks 15-16 deferrals: child env fingerprint vs live process env / tool binding (AK-028), runner resolution in doctor check 3, concrete runners.default"
    - "Task 17/27 deferrals: produced_at integer vs Annex-B string placeholder in schemas"
    - "Task 20 deferrals: payment unification (critic costs into run budget_spent), model-rung dispatch unmetered, workspace-root pairing library seam, L4 cohort non-separability fixture, evidence production binding first-facet bytes"
    - "Task 22/24 deferrals: reference candidate recording / mutation teeth"
    - "Task 25 deferrals: evidence-fs crash injection E2E"
    - "Ports revision deferrals: BudgetMeter::mint type-level seal, checkpoint-only run projection enum surface, Option facet fields, ladder rungs 5-9/11, locator contract-defined matching for non-deterministic kinds — plus two opened by Task 13: a typed durable residual-row read (condition 4's durable half currently grounds on the checkpoint projection) and ReferenceVersion.evidence_ref (N1, re-grounded to the first in-type consumer)"
    - "Arch-suite standing trigger DISCHARGED 2026-08-27 (Task 13 B3 touch): E4/F1/F3, B.5a masked spellings, A5.2 allowlist granularity, B-F16 shapes all re-litigated and HOLD; B-F16's production-instance inventory re-recorded (.agents/reports/task13/arch-relitigation.md). The obligation REBIRTHS at the next arch-suite touch."
  warnings:
    # Anything that could cause a resuming agent to do real damage if
    # missed — wrong resident state, an action explicitly out of scope
    # until a later task, an irreversible operation to avoid. Only put
    # things here that are genuinely dangerous to miss, not routine notes.
    - "Never edit .wayfinder/answer-key.md or reference.lock — ruler is frozen; check with `just ruler` before and after every task."
    - "Do not implement directly as orchestrator while delegation is available (AGENTS.md rule); maintain strict blind critic separation."
    - "Only one agent may compile at a time (build-lock discipline); WSL2 host memory is tight (~1.6 GiB free); watch target/ size and keep max_parallel low."
    - "Never mark a task settled on builder say-so; settlement requires independent blind confirmation (peer/adversarial CONFIRM) and proven teeth."
    - "Always reconcile `git status` vs CURRENT_STATUS.yml vs IN-FLIGHT.md before treating any slice as unstarted (tree outranks record)."
    - "One task, one commit discipline: use explicit pathspecs and never stage .jolli/, .tmp/, .agents/prompts/, or operator edits."